Note: the Windows profile registry entry for %1 could not be removed yet.\n\nThe profile DIRECTORY is gone. Windows still holds the registry record of it,\nand if an account called %1 is created again before that record clears,\nWindows honours it and gives the account a DIFFERENT home directory -\nC:\Users\%1 with a suffix added - so anything expected in the old one, ssh\nkeys included, will not be found there.\n\nSD has recorded it. THE NEXT TIME THIS COMPUTER STARTS, the SD service\nremoves the record; nothing else has to be done. CREATE.ACCOUNT refuses the\nname in the meantime rather than let the wrong home be assigned quietly.\n\nAn administrator can also clear it now: "Get-CimInstance Win32_UserProfile"\nfrom an elevated prompt lists the orphaned profile, and "Remove-CimInstance"\non the entry whose LocalPath is the old home directory removes it.
